Subject: [PATCH] Replace BESOS/harlow/TensorFlow in surrogate modelling with
 bdopt

- surrogate notebook template and backend/inject_data.py now use bdopt (load_idf, AdaptiveSampler, GP/MLP/PyTorch surrogates, NSGA-II)
- new bdopt_Example_N.ipynb for the seven surrogate examples (generated from the Harlow ones, executed with a reduced budget on EnergyPlus 9.6)
- dedicated surrogate image (conda-environment/surrogate, Python 3.11, EnergyPlus inside the image) and compose service
- besos, harlow and tensorflow-probability removed from the shared Python 3.9 conda environment

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VTMtxNYXAoqPsqUJp3EcyK
