+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "# Surrogate modelling and design optimisation with bdopt\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Model `lab_building.idf`, weather `Torino_IT-hour.epw`.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The notebook builds a surrogate of the EnergyPlus model with **adaptive sampling** (simulations are placed where the surrogate needs them), compares surrogate models and runs a multi-objective optimisation on the best one. It uses the `bdopt` library (EnergyPlus 8.7+, no BESOS, no TensorFlow)."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "74b712c4",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import warnings\n",
+    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
+    "%matplotlib inline\n",
+    "\n",
+    "import numpy as np\n",
+    "import pandas as pd\n",
+    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
+    "\n",
+    "from bdopt import (CategoryParameter, EnergyPlusEvaluator, FieldSelector, IntegerParameter,\n",
+    "                   Parameter, Problem, RangeParameter, load_idf)\n",
+    "from bdopt.adaptive import AdaptiveSampler\n",
+    "from bdopt.optimize import nsga2\n",
+    "from bdopt.surrogate import GPSurrogate, MLPSurrogate, TorchMLP\n",
+    "from bdopt import viz"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "dfe68999",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Budget"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "cb9c0974",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "# Budget of the study (EnergyPlus simulations are the expensive part).\n",
+    "N_INITIAL = 20    # first Latin-hypercube simulations\n",
+    "N_TEST = 5          # held-out simulations used to measure the surrogate error\n",
+    "MAX_ITER = 40      # adaptive iterations (batch of new simulations each)\n",
+    "BATCH = 1\n",
+    "TOL = 0.05                 # stop when the test error (in std units of each objective) is below this\n",
+    "PROCESSES = 1    # parallel EnergyPlus runs"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "163b76f3",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Model and weather"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "41e14adb",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "building = load_idf(\"lab_building.idf\")\n",
+    "epw_file = \"Torino_IT-hour.epw\"\n",
+    "print(building)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "0e543b17",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Design space\n",
+    "Where each design variable is written in the IDF (`FieldSelector`) and the values it can take (`RangeParameter`, `CategoryParameter`, `IntegerParameter`)."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "491a1971",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "roof_ins = FieldSelector(class_name='Material',\n",
+    "                         object_name='MW Glass Wool (rolls)_.1445',\n",
+    "                         field_name='Thickness')\n",
+    "wall_ins = FieldSelector(class_name='Material', \n",
+    "                         object_name='EPS Expanded Polystyrene (Heavyweight)_.1', \n",
+    "                         field_name='Thickness')\n",
+    "\n",
+    "wall_range = RangeParameter(min_val=0.1,max_val=0.5)\n",
+    "roof_range = RangeParameter(min_val=0.1,max_val=0.8)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "insulation_param = [Parameter(selector=wall_ins,\n",
+    "                                 value_descriptor=wall_range ,\n",
+    "                                 name='Wall Insulation'),\n",
+    "                   Parameter(selector=roof_ins,\n",
+    "                                 value_descriptor=roof_range ,\n",
+    "                                 name='Roof Insulation')]"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "45b51fcd",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "ventAchRange = RangeParameter(min_val = 0.0, max_val=6.0)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "ventilationAchParam = []\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "ventACH_sel = FieldSelector(class_name = 'ZoneVentilation:DesignFlowRate', \n",
+    "                    object_name = '*', \n",
+    "                    field_name = 'Air Changes per Hour')\n",
+    "ventilationAchParam.append(Parameter(selector=ventACH_sel, \n",
+    "                                     value_descriptor=ventAchRange, \n",
+    "                                     name='Ventilation ACH'))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "8dae74a9",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "lights_selector = FieldSelector(class_name='Lights', object_name='*', field_name='Watts per Zone Floor Area')\n",
+    "lights_range = RangeParameter(min_val=5,max_val=20)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "lights_param =     Parameter(\n",
+    "        lights_selector,\n",
+    "        value_descriptor=lights_range ,\n",
+    "        name=\"Lights Watts/Area\",\n",
+    "    )"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "fff2616c",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "TempShadingRange = RangeParameter(min_val = 18, max_val=30)\n",
+    "RadShadingRange = RangeParameter(min_val = 30, max_val=300)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "setpointParams = []\n",
+    "shade_setpoint_sel = FieldSelector(class_name ='WindowShadingControl', \n",
+    "                    object_name = '*', \n",
+    "                    field_name='Setpoint' )\n",
+    "shade_setpoint2_sel = FieldSelector(class_name ='WindowShadingControl', \n",
+    "                     object_name = '*', \n",
+    "                     field_name='Setpoint 2' )\n",
+    "setpointParams.append(Parameter(selector=shade_setpoint_sel, value_descriptor = TempShadingRange, name='Temp Setpoint shading'))\n",
+    "setpointParams.append(Parameter(selector=shade_setpoint2_sel, value_descriptor = RadShadingRange, name='Rad Setpoint shading'))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "fe5d5f11",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "# One categorical design variable shared by every window of the model.\n",
+    "# (The BESOS notebook created one variable per window, all called 'Windows types'; the model\n",
+    "#  has 9 windows, which would be 9 identically named variables.)\n",
+    "win_arr = ['single_glazing', 'double_glazing', 'triple_glazing']\n",
+    "windowsParam = Parameter(\n",
+    "    selector=FieldSelector(class_name='FenestrationSurface:Detailed', object_name='*',\n",
+    "                           field_name='Construction Name', where={'Surface Type': 'Window'}),\n",
+    "    value_descriptor=CategoryParameter(win_arr),\n",
+    "    name='Windows types',\n",
+    ")\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "fded7e9b",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "parameters = insulation_param + [windowsParam] + [lights_param] + ventilationAchParam + setpointParams"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "a297def6",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "objectives = ['Electricity:Facility','DistrictHeating:Facility','DistrictCooling:Facility']"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "7f8883c6",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Problem and evaluator"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "59bbe159",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "problem = Problem(parameters, objectives)       # parameters + objectives; bounds/order/scaling are derived from it\n",
+    "print(problem)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "# EnergyPlus is found automatically (the installed version that matches the model); results are\n",
+    "# cached on disk, so re-running a cell or resuming after a crash never repeats a simulation.\n",
+    "evaluator = EnergyPlusEvaluator(problem, building, epw_file, out_dir=\"outputdir\", processes=PROCESSES)\n",
+    "print(evaluator.eplus)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "ff019b00",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Adaptive sampling"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "21037eae",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "sampler = AdaptiveSampler(problem, evaluator, method=\"flola_voronoi\", seed=0)\n",
+    "result = sampler.run(n_initial=N_INITIAL, n_test=N_TEST, max_iter=MAX_ITER, batch=BATCH, tol=TOL)\n",
+    "print(result)\n",
+    "result.data.to_pickle(\"adaptive_samples.pkl\")     # EnergyPlus runs (inputs + outputs), in real units\n",
+    "result.test.to_pickle(\"test_samples.pkl\")\n",
+    "print(evaluator.stats())\n",
+    "result.history"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "ec26882e",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Samples"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "ea5b3730",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "viz.convergence(result.history, tol=TOL)\n",
+    "viz.pairplot(result.data, problem)\n",
+    "viz.correlation_heatmap(result.data, problem)\n",
+    "result.data.describe()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "1aff5c94",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Surrogate models"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "ee409612",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "# Same data, three surrogate models; no manual scaling: inputs live in [0,1], outputs are standardised inside.\n",
+    "models = {\n",
+    "    \"Gaussian process\": GPSurrogate(),\n",
+    "    \"MLP (scikit-learn)\": MLPSurrogate(),\n",
+    "    \"MLP (PyTorch)\": TorchMLP(hidden=(32, 64, 32), n_ensemble=3),\n",
+    "}\n",
+    "scores = {}\n",
+    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
+    "    model.fit(result.data, problem)\n",
+    "    scores[name] = model.score(result.test)\n",
+    "    print(name); display(scores[name][[\"rmse_pct\", \"cv_rmse\", \"nmbe\", \"r2\"]].round(3))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "d06c44cd",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "summary = pd.DataFrame({name: s[\"rmse_pct\"] for name, s in scores.items()})\n",
+    "display(summary.round(3))                       # RMSE as % of the mean, per objective\n",
+    "best_name = summary.mean().idxmin()\n",
+    "surrogate = models[best_name]\n",
+    "print(\"selected surrogate:\", best_name)\n",
+    "viz.parity(result.test[problem.objective_names], surrogate.predict(result.test))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "c02e193b",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Optimisation"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "9595bb67",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "# Multi-objective optimisation (NSGA-II) on the surrogate: thousands of designs in seconds.\n",
+    "front = nsga2(problem, surrogate, pop_size=100, n_gen=100, seed=0)\n",
+    "print(len(front), \"non-dominated designs\")\n",
+    "front.df"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "2798d983",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Selected design"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "2fadf371",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "best = front.closest_to_ideal()                 # closest to the ideal point after min-max scaling\n",
+    "display(best.to_frame(\"selected design\"))\n",
+    "viz.pareto(front, background=result.data, highlight=best)\n",
+    "viz.parallel_coordinates(front.df, problem)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "# Check the selected design with the real simulator.\n",
+    "x = best[problem.parameter_names].to_frame().T.reset_index(drop=True)\n",
+    "pd.DataFrame({\"EnergyPlus\": evaluator.evaluate(x).iloc[0], \"surrogate\": surrogate.predict(x).iloc[0]})"
+   ]
+  }
+ ],
